 et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000164181"],"dataset_symbols":["ELOVL7"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/ELOVL7","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"ELOVL7","gene_symbol_current":"ELOVL7","gene_id":"ENSG00000164181","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.157391,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.020518,"nucleus_score":-1.6,"pct_ad":0.129013,"pct_control":0.137103,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.986149,"donor_log2fc":-0.0490483,"donor_lfcse":0.0993773,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-2.5922e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"ELOVL7","gene_symbol_current":"ELOVL7","gene_id":"ENSG00000164181","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.795115,"donor_log2fc":-0.171423,"donor_lfcse":0.135795,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00910355}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000164181","module":"brown","kme":0.152484,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.372712,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000164181","entrez_id":["79993"],"uniprot":["A1L3X0"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables fatty acid elongase activity. Involved in fatty acid elongation, polyunsaturated fatty acid; fatty acid elongation, saturated fatty acid; and very long-chain fatty acid biosynthetic process. Located in endoplasmic reticulum. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"A1L3X0","text":"Catalyzes the first and rate-limiting reaction of the four reactions that constitute the long-chain fatty acids elongation cycle. This endoplasmic reticulum-bound enzymatic process allows the addition of 2 carbons to the chain of long- and very long-chain fatty acids (VLCFAs) per cycle. Condensing enzyme with higher activity toward C18 acyl-CoAs, especially C18:3(n-3) acyl-CoAs and C18:3(n-6)-CoAs. Also active toward C20:4-, C18:0-, C18:1-, C18:2- and C16:0-CoAs, and weakly toward C20:0-CoA. Little or no activity toward C22:0-, C24:0-, or C26:0-CoAs. May participate in the production of saturated and polyunsaturated VLCFAs of different chain lengths that are involved in multiple biological processes as precursors of membrane lipids and lipid mediators."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}